<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Urus Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1377">1377</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Urus Khan was a Jochid ruler of the White Horde, in the eastern part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>, from about 1368 until his death in 1377. He sought to reunite the Golden Horde and briefly held its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarai">Sarai</a>, but was challenged by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokhtamysh">Tokhtamysh</a>, who was backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>. His descendants Kerei and Janibek founded the Kazakh Khanate around 1465, and later Kazakh khans traced their line to him.</p></div>
